            <div xml:id="d214">

                <pb facs="0364" n="270" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg270"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 L 36/154: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Chargé in Greece</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Atherton</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-03-17T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 17,
                                1924—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>37. Our no. 32 of March 10, 4 p.m. and your no. 50 of March 12, 10 p.m. The
                    Department approved your suggestion for short delay in requesting <hi
                        rendition="#italic">agrément</hi> for Laughlin, but considering time which
                    has passed since the change of Ministry and since events reported in your
                    telegram no. 50, you are now instructed to carry out the instructions given in
                    our telegram no. 32.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
